    "kok_maddesi": "Back to library EtymArab TQY تقي BP – • HDAL • © SG | 15Feb2021 √TQY “root” ▪ TQY_1 comprising items like the vn.s tuqàⁿ ~ taqwà ‘godliness, devoutness, piety’ and taqiyyaẗ ‘fear, caution, prudence; (in Shiitic Islam) dissimulation of one’s religion’ as well as the adj.s taqīy and muttaqīⁿ ‘godfearing, godly, devout, pious’, the latter a PA of the vb. VIII (Gt-stem) ĭttaqà ‘to fear ( allāhᵃ God)’: in most dictionaries √TQY is considered to be a secondary development, based on the Gt-stem of ↗WQY Other values, now obsolete (Hava1899): ▪ † TQY_2 ‘corn-seed’: † taqāwà ; cf. also D-stem vb. † taqqà (II) ‘to sow (corn-seeds)’ ▪ † TQY_3 ‘fat (man)’: † muttaqīⁿ ▪ † TQY_ ‘…’: † … ▪ TQY_1: √TQY is usually regarded to be a secondary “root”, a back formation from ↗WQY via the latter’s Gt-stem in ĭttaqà in which the first radical w has been assimilated to the infixed ‑t‑ ( ĭttaqà ĭWtaQà ); the form ĭttaqà was then interpreted as if from * ĭTtaQà . ▪ † TQY_2: ? ▪ † TQY_3: ? – prob. fig. from muttaqīⁿ ‘godfearing, godly, devout, pious’ (TQY_1), though, if valid, semantics remain unclear. ▪ TQY_1 † taqà (for ĭttaqà WQY) ‘to fear, honour (God); to guard against’ – Hava1899 ▪ … ▪ TQY_1: ↗WQY ▪ † TQY_2: … ▪ † TQY_3: ↗TQY_1 / WQY ? ▪ TQY _1: see obove, section CONC. ▪ † TQY_2: … ▪ † TQY_3: … ▪ … – – Sources ; meta ; gram ; engl ; conc ; hist ; cogn ; disc ; west ; deriv ;",
